{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01579ijkPseJGyq2DeL3ToxW","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd087-sizeparse\n2\ttitle: \"pkg/sizeparse: Size String Parser with Unit Suffixes\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Eight cmd/ utilities (head, tail, split, truncate, numfmt, du, sort, od) need to parse\n6\t  size strings with unit suffixes (K, M, G, T for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers\n7\t  of 1000; b for 512). In run 37, each utility independently implemented suffix parsing\n8\t  with slight variations, totaling ~50 lines per utility. This duplication risks\n9\t  inconsistent suffix handling across utilities.\n10\t\n11\t  pkg/sizeparse provides a single parser that handles all GNU coreutils suffix\n12\t  conventions. Each cmd/ utility imports this package instead of reimplementing suffix\n13\t  multiplication.\n14\t\n15\tgoals:\n16\t  - G1: Parse size strings with binary (IEC) and decimal (SI) unit suffixes.\n17\t  - G2: Support the full GNU coreutils suffix set including b, K, KiB, KB, M, MiB, MB, G, GiB, GB, T, TiB, TB, P, PiB, PB, E, EiB, EB, Z, ZiB, ZB, Y, YiB, YB.\n18\t  - G3: Support optional sign prefixes (+, -) for relative size adjustments.\n19\t\n20\trequirements:\n21\t  R1:\n22\t    title: Size parsing\n23\t    items:\n24\t      - R1.1:\n25\t          text: |\n26\t            Must provide func Parse(s string) (int64, error) that parses a size string\n27\t            consisting of an optional sign (+ or -), a decimal integer, and an optional\n28\t            unit suffix. Returns the size in bytes. Returns an error for invalid input.\n29\t      - R1.2:\n30\t          text: |\n31\t            Must support binary (IEC) suffixes: K or KiB (1024), M or MiB (1024^2),\n32\t            G or GiB (1024^3), T or TiB (1024^4), P or PiB (1024^5), E or EiB (1024^6),\n33\t            Z or ZiB (1024^7), Y or YiB (1024^8). Must also support b (512) for\n34\t            POSIX compatibility.\n35\t      - R1.3:\n36\t          text: |\n37\t            Must support decimal (SI) suffixes: KB (1000), MB (1000^2), GB (1000^3),\n38\t            TB (1000^4), PB (1000^5), EB (1000^6), ZB (1000^7), YB (1000^8).\n39\t      - R1.4:\n40\t          text: Must preserve the sign in the returned value. \"+100K\" returns +102400, \"-50M\" returns -52428800. No sign prefix means positive.\n41\t\n42\t  R2:\n43\t    title: Extended parsing options\n44\t    items:\n45\t      - R2.1:\n46\t          text: |\n47\t            Must provide func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\n48\t            where ParseOptions allows configuring behavior:\n49\t\n50\t              type ParseOptions struct {\n51\t                  AllowSign    bool // allow +/- prefix (default false for Parse)\n52\t                  DefaultUnit  int64 // multiplier when no suffix given (default 1)\n53\t              }\n54\t      - R2.2:\n55\t          text: \"ParseWithOptions with DefaultUnit=1024 and input '5' returns 5120 (5 * 1024). This supports utilities like du where the default unit is blocks.\"\n56\t\n57\t  R3:\n58\t    title: Constraints\n59\t    items:\n60\t      - R3.1:\n61\t          text: Must return an error when the numeric part overflows int64.\n62\t      - R3.2:\n63\t          text: Must return an error when the suffix is not recognized.\n64\t\n65\tnon_goals:\n66\t  - pkg/sizeparse does not format sizes for output; use pkg/format.HumanSize for that.\n67\t  - pkg/sizeparse does not handle floating-point sizes.\n68\t\n69\tpackage_contract:\n70\t  exports:\n71\t    - name: ParseOptions\n72\t      signature: \"type ParseOptions struct { AllowSign bool; DefaultUnit int64 }\"\n73\t    - name: Parse\n74\t      signature: \"func Parse(s string) (int64, error)\"\n75\t    - name: ParseWithOptions\n76\t      signature: \"func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\"\n77\t  imports:\n78\t    - fmt\n79\t    - strconv\n80\t    - strings\n81\t  import_constraints:\n82\t    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n83\t    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n84\t\n85\tacceptance_criteria:\n86\t  - id: AC1\n87\t    criterion: \"Parse('100K') returns 102400.\"\n88\t    traces:\n89\t      - R1.1\n90\t      - R1.2\n91\t  - id: AC2\n92\t    criterion: \"Parse('5MB') returns 5000000.\"\n93\t    traces:\n94\t      - R1.1\n95\t      - R1.3\n96\t  - id: AC3\n97\t    criterion: \"ParseWithOptions('+50M', ParseOptions{AllowSign: true}) returns 52428800.\"\n98\t    traces:\n99\t      - R1.4\n100\t      - R2.1\n101\t  - id: AC4\n102\t    criterion: \"Parse('invalid') returns an error.\"\n103\t    traces:\n104\t      - R3.2\n105\t  - id: AC5\n106\t    criterion: \"pkg/sizeparse compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n107\t    traces:\n108\t      - R1.1\n109\t      - R1.2\n110\t      - R1.3\n111\t      - R1.4\n112\t      - R2.1\n113\t      - R2.2\n114\t      - R3.1\n115\t      - R3.2\n116\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd36bd82-f87c-4c2e-a83c-5a6adb893e8d","uuid":"09d593e7-1aaf-43a1-b8b2-5e4c67715acf","timestamp":"2026-04-19T18:52:55.420Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5014/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd087-sizeparse.yaml","content":"id: srd087-sizeparse\ntitle: \"pkg/sizeparse: Size String Parser with Unit Suffixes\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Eight cmd/ utilities (head, tail, split, truncate, numfmt, du, sort, od) need to parse\n  size strings with unit suffixes (K, M, G, T for powers of 1024; KB, MB, GB for powers\n  of 1000; b for 512). In run 37, each utility independently implemented suffix parsing\n  with slight variations, totaling ~50 lines per utility. This duplication risks\n  inconsistent suffix handling across utilities.\n\n  pkg/sizeparse provides a single parser that handles all GNU coreutils suffix\n  conventions. Each cmd/ utility imports this package instead of reimplementing suffix\n  multiplication.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Parse size strings with binary (IEC) and decimal (SI) unit suffixes.\n  - G2: Support the full GNU coreutils suffix set including b, K, KiB, KB, M, MiB, MB, G, GiB, GB, T, TiB, TB, P, PiB, PB, E, EiB, EB, Z, ZiB, ZB, Y, YiB, YB.\n  - G3: Support optional sign prefixes (+, -) for relative size adjustments.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Size parsing\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide func Parse(s string) (int64, error) that parses a size string\n            consisting of an optional sign (+ or -), a decimal integer, and an optional\n            unit suffix. Returns the size in bytes. Returns an error for invalid input.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: |\n            Must support binary (IEC) suffixes: K or KiB (1024), M or MiB (1024^2),\n            G or GiB (1024^3), T or TiB (1024^4), P or PiB (1024^5), E or EiB (1024^6),\n            Z or ZiB (1024^7), Y or YiB (1024^8). Must also support b (512) for\n            POSIX compatibility.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: |\n            Must support decimal (SI) suffixes: KB (1000), MB (1000^2), GB (1000^3),\n            TB (1000^4), PB (1000^5), EB (1000^6), ZB (1000^7), YB (1000^8).\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must preserve the sign in the returned value. \"+100K\" returns +102400, \"-50M\" returns -52428800. No sign prefix means positive.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Extended parsing options\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\n            where ParseOptions allows configuring behavior:\n\n              type ParseOptions struct {\n                  AllowSign    bool // allow +/- prefix (default false for Parse)\n                  DefaultUnit  int64 // multiplier when no suffix given (default 1)\n              }\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"ParseWithOptions with DefaultUnit=1024 and input '5' returns 5120 (5 * 1024). This supports utilities like du where the default unit is blocks.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Constraints\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: Must return an error when the numeric part overflows int64.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must return an error when the suffix is not recognized.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - pkg/sizeparse does not format sizes for output; use pkg/format.HumanSize for that.\n  - pkg/sizeparse does not handle floating-point sizes.\n\npackage_contract:\n  exports:\n    - name: ParseOptions\n      signature: \"type ParseOptions struct { AllowSign bool; DefaultUnit int64 }\"\n    - name: Parse\n      signature: \"func Parse(s string) (int64, error)\"\n    - name: ParseWithOptions\n      signature: \"func ParseWithOptions(s string, opts ParseOptions) (int64, error)\"\n  imports:\n    - fmt\n    - strconv\n    - strings\n  import_constraints:\n    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"Parse('100K') returns 102400.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"Parse('5MB') returns 5000000.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.3\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"ParseWithOptions('+50M', ParseOptions{AllowSign: true}) returns 52428800.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Parse('invalid') returns an error.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.2\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"pkg/sizeparse compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n","numLines":116,"startLine":1,"totalLines":116}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HYfrZamwkuyxy3VzBWLCDu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the full requirements. Looking at the existing code, I need to:\n\n1. R2.1/R2.2: ParseWithOptions already works for AllowSign and DefaultUnit - the existing code handles these correctly.\n2. R3.1: Overflow detection - need to check if `num * multiplier` overflows int64.\n3. R3.2: Unknown suffix error - already handled.\n\nThe task requirements say:\n- R1: AllowSign true accepts +/- signs - already works\n- R2: DefaultUnit - already works\n- R3: Error handling for empty/non-numeric/unknown suffix - already works\n\n\n- R4: Overflow detection - needs implementation\n\nI'm noticing a discrepancy in the SRD though. R1.1 says Parse should accept an optional sign, but the current implementation sets AllowSign to false. The task description treats this as R2.1 behavior for ParseWithOptions with AllowSign true, so I need to clarify whether Parse itself should allow signs or if that's only for ParseWithOptions.\n\nLooking at the actual requirements: R1 needs ParseWithOptions with AllowSign working (done), R2 needs DefaultUnit (done), R3 needs error handling (done), and R4 needs overflow detection added. I should also remove the TODO comment from ParseWithOptions.\n\nFor overflow detection, I need to safely check if multiplying the parsed number by its unit multiplier would overflow int64 - the key is checking whether the result would exceed the maximum int64 value before actually performing the multiplication.\n\nWriting the updated parse.go with overflow detection...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1783,"cache_read_input_tokens":65847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1783},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"